From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - retry queued mailbox messages after each response

The PDC mailbox returns -ENOSPC from send_data when its rings are full.
The mailbox framework then keeps the message queued and tries it again
only when the next tx done is signalled. This driver signals tx done
itself, in mailbox_send_message() right after each send. A message that
did not fit therefore waits for another request to be sent. If none
comes, for example at the end of a burst, the request never completes.

Each response frees ring space. Signal tx done when a request completes,
so the framework sends the next queued message. A request that sends
another chunk already signals tx done in mailbox_send_message().

Fixes: f0e2ce58f853 ("crypto: brcm - Explicity ACK mailbox message")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -1652,6 +1652,7 @@ static void spu_rx_callback(struct mbox_client *cl, void *msg)
 	struct spu_hw *spu = &iproc_priv.spu;
 	struct brcm_message *mssg = msg;
 	struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx;
+	u8 chan_idx;
 	int err;
 
 	rctx = mssg->ctx;
@@ -1660,6 +1661,7 @@ static void spu_rx_callback(struct mbox_client *cl, void *msg)
 		pr_err("%s(): no request context", __func__);
 		return;
 	}
+	chan_idx = rctx->chan_idx;
 
 	err = mssg->error;
 	if (unlikely(err))
@@ -1727,6 +1729,8 @@ static void spu_rx_callback(struct mbox_client *cl, void *msg)
 
 cb_finish:
 	finish_req(rctx, err);
+
+	mbox_client_txdone(iproc_priv.mbox[chan_idx], 0);
 }
 
 /* ==================== Kernel Cryptographic API ==================== */
